  "summary": "CRC outreach worklist for 'Okafor CRC 2026' (grp-okafor-crc, 5 members) worked under RBC-QM-02. The measurement period is calendar year 2026.\n\n| Patient | Age at end of 2026 | Status | Reason | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| pt-0009 Elly Trantow | 72 | Open gap | No qualifying screening on record. Not excluded: her only Frailty diagnosis (cond-00189) was marked entered in error today (Dr. Lin, comm-00301). That removes the age-66+ frailty + advanced illness exclusion, even though she takes donepezil. No nursing home, hospice/palliative care or colorectal cancer. | FIT kit sr-t0001 ordered; outreach message comm-t0005 sent |\n| pt-0020 Kelsie Rohan | 52 | Excluded | Hospice episode 2026-06-16 to 2026-08-21 (eoc-00002, finished; confirmed by discharge summary doc-00402). Hospice at any point in 2026 excludes her, even though she later revoked it for a clinical trial. | None (no order, no contact) |\n| pt-0022 Tiny Koss | 52 | Open gap | Her only FIT (obs-01732) was corrected today: collected 2025-12-31, not 2026-01-05, so it falls outside 2026. No colonoscopy, sigmoidoscopy, CT colonography or sDNA-FIT on record. No exclusions (her past cancers were of the mouth, not colorectal). | FIT kit sr-t0002 ordered; message comm-t0006 sent |\n| pt-0024 Delaine MacGyver | 51 | Open gap | Her 2024-06-11 sDNA-FIT (obs-01871) was withdrawn by Harbor Lab for a labelling error and is entered in error (doc-00401). Her 2025 colonoscopy order (sr-00003) was never done, and an order is not screening. No exclusions. No active FIT order existed. | FIT kit sr-t0003 ordered; message comm-t0007 sent |\n| pt-0073 Marisol Quintero | 58 | Open gap | Her FIT dated 2026-01-08 (obs-73001) was cancelled as entered in error. The re-issued report (obs-05001, doc-00403) shows it was collected 2025-12-28, outside 2026. No other screening and no exclusions. | FIT kit sr-t0004 ordered; message comm-t0008 sent |\n\nAll 5 members are in the age 46–75 population. Each FIT order window runs 2026-10-23 to 2026-12-31. Each message says the kit is on its way and explains how to collect, label and mail back the sample before year end. The messages say nothing about earlier tests.\n\nArrivals: five items reached the inbox as work started: Dr. Lin's frailty correction (pt-0009), the hospice discharge summary (pt-0020), the corrected FIT (pt-0022), the sDNA withdrawal notice (pt-0024) and the FIT re-issue (pt-0073). I read all five before deciding anything, so no decision needed correcting. Each item is closed with the reason recorded and the order and message linked. No other new items arrived. The older inbox items unrelated to this worklist were left untouched.",
